#: ../../docstring
#: ../../source/generated/modules/freeports.cli.rst:18:<autosummary>:1
#: freeports.cli.FreeportsFileConfig:1 of
msgid "The Python shim of the configuration file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.cli.FreeportsFileConfig:3 of
msgid ""
"It exposes only what callers really read from it: where to find it, which"
" input database and formats repository it declares, and the two tooling "
"sections that `freeports-dev` and `freeports-validate` are configured "
"through. It is not the complete resolved configuration, which is the "
"result of merging every source and makes no sense to build from Python."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.cli.FreeportsFileConfig:8 of
msgid ""
"This class is the whole reason the two tooling commands need no "
"configuration machinery of their own: finding the file, deciding which "
"tier wins and refusing an unknown key all happen once, in Rust, and both "
"commands read the answer from here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.cli.FreeportsFileConfig:12 of
msgid ""
"Every getter is upper-case and flat, so the three names for one setting "
"differ only in punctuation: `dev.page_type` in the file, "
"`FREEPORTS_DEV_PAGE_TYPE` in the environment, `DEV_PAGE_TYPE` here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.cli.FreeportsFileConfig.DEV_NOCONFIRM:1 of
msgid "`dev.noconfirm` — skip the `make-tests` confirmation prompts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.cli.FreeportsFileConfig.DEV_PAGE_TYPE:1 of
msgid ""
"`dev.page_type` — the default page type for `make-tests` and `inspect-"
"page`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.cli.FreeportsFileConfig.DEV_TARGET_LISTS:1 of
msgid "`dev.target_lists` — the lists a format repository's own tests search for."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.cli.FreeportsFileConfig.INPUT_DB_PATH:1 of
msgid ""
"The name is upper-cased, as configuration keys were exposed as upper-case"
" attributes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.cli.FreeportsFileConfig.VALIDATE_DEEP:1 of
msgid ""
"`validate.deep` — also verify the resources a methodology page pins by "
"sub-hash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.cli.FreeportsFileConfig.VALIDATE_KEY_ID:1 of
msgid "`validate.key_id` — the GPG key grants are signed with."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.cli.FreeportsFileConfig.VALIDATE_OFFLINE:1 of
msgid ""
"`validate.offline` — never fetch a methodology page; answer from the "
"cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.cli.FreeportsFileConfig.VALIDATE_SOURCES:1 of
msgid ""
"`validate.sources` — where methodology pages are resolved from, in "
"priority order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.cli.FreeportsFileConfig.VALIDATE_SOURCES:3 of
msgid ""
"A list, and handed over as one: `freeports-validate` resolves a name from"
" the first source that offers it, so the order this arrives in is the "
"order the file was written in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.cli.FreeportsFileConfig.find_config:1 of
msgid ""
"The configuration file to read: working directory, then user tier, then "
"system tier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring cli.run_job:3 of
msgid ""
"The entry point of the development tooling's integration tests: it takes "
"primitive arguments instead of parsed command-line ones, skips the merge "
"of the configuration sources — there are none here — and calls the same "
"job run and result write the command line does."
msgstr ""

